usage: mpublish [options] condor_or_crab_dirs

mpublish: get the staged-out files from condor/crab directories and print out
lines for SampleFiles.py

positional arguments:
  condor_or_crab_dirs   The condor/crab directories.

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --dataset DATASET     The dataset name to use.
  --blacklist [BLACKLIST [BLACKLIST ...]]
                        Don't include files that match these patterns (default
                        ['vertex_histos*root']).
  --pattern PATTERN     Glob-style pattern to filter the files, useful if
                        there are multiple files output per job.
  --partial             If set, partial publishing is allowed.
  --only-done           If set, only look at dirs with the mmon_done marker
                        file.
  --no-coderep          whether to disable coderep output
  --no-lpc-shortcut     whether to use the lpc shortcut on crab dirs
  --no-dbs              whether to use information from dbs
  --nevents-per-job NEVENTS_PER_JOB
                        nevents to use if reading dbs fails
  --include-condor-nevents
                        If set, parse xmls to get nevents from condor wds.
  --from-merge          Input is from merge jobs (implies --partial and --no-
                        coderep).
